I have never seen that specific problem, but often Jaws will read text
from a previous line when it encounters a blank line, or it will read
the title and size of the file at the end of every line, or any one of
several random and non-reproduceable bugs that have been with me for
many years. It does similar things in Notepad, so it is not specific
to edSharp, or so it seems.
That said, try insert-s a few times; you may have it set to all,
instead of none or highlighted, and that sometimes messes things up.

